& =151.2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the final answer is $151.2.$" 13194139539471 17592186576411 true] [17592186609859 1071 "A toy store sold $250$ puzzles in June. In July, sales are $140%$ greater than in June. How many puzzles did the toy store sell in July?\n\nThe toy store sold\n{{field-1}}\npuzzles in July." 13194139539471 17592186576411 false] [17592186609859 1071 "A toy store sold $250$ puzzles in June. In July, sales are $140\\%$ greater than in June. How many puzzles did the toy store sell in July?\n\nThe toy store sold\n{{field-1}}\npuzzles in July." 13194139539471 17592186576411 true] [17592186609859 1074 "To find July's sales, we apply a $140%$ increase to June's figure.\n\nIncreasing by $140%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+140%=240%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n240%=\\frac{240}{100}=2.4\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original amount by $2.4:$\n\n$$\n250\\times 2.4=600\n$$\n\nSo, the toy store sold $600$ puzzles in July." 13194139539471 17592186576411 false] [17592186609859 1074 "To find July's sales, we apply a $140\\%$ increase to June's figure.\n\nIncreasing by $140\\%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100\\%+140\\%=240\\%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n240\\%=\\frac{240}{100}=2.4\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original amount by $2.4:$\n\n$$\n250\\times 2.4=600\n$$\n\nSo, the toy store sold $600$ puzzles in July." 13194139539471 17592186576411 true] [17592186609868 1071 "There were approximately $58,\\,000$ students enrolled at a university in $2022.$ Enrollment planners predict that this number will grow by $22%$ by the year $2025.$ Which of the following is closest to the projected enrollment in $2025?$" 13194139539471 17592186576411 false] [17592186609868 1071 "There were approximately $58,\\,000$ students enrolled at a university in $2022.$ Enrollment planners predict that this number will grow by $22\\%$ by the year $2025.$ Whic